<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><documents xmlns:xsi = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation = "HDocumentSchema.xsd"><document type = "H"><pnldref>H12087</pnldref><english><title>Member of a jury engage in prohibited conduct</title><additionalkeywords><additionalkeyword>Juries Act 1974</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>served</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>trial</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>tries</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>try</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>case</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>cases</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>court</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>issue</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>google</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>googled</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>defendant</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>research</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>researched</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>internet</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>look up</additionalkeyword></additionalkeywords><standardoffencewording>On **(..SPECIFY DATE..) at **(..SPECIFY TOWNSHIP..), being a member of a jury that tried an issue in a case before a court, namely **(..SPECIFY CASE AND COURT..), intentionally engaged in prohibited conduct during the trial period, in that you **(..SPECIFY DETAILS OF PROHIBITED CONDUCT..)</standardoffencewording><legislation>Contrary to section 20C of the Juries Act 1974.</legislation><pointstoprove>date and location&lt;br /&gt;member of a jury that tried an issue in a case before a court &lt;br /&gt;intentionally engaged in prohibited conduct during trial period</pointstoprove><investigatoractions><investigatoraction><code>IA1</code><description>Fingerprint and photograph</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA2</code><description>DNA Samples: If crime scene stain present - take evidential sample If no crime scene stain and DNA not confirmed on PNC - take Criminal Justice sample. If DNA confirmed on PNC - CJ sample not required</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA27</code><description>Confirm proposed charge is appropriately authorised (Police or CPS)</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA28</code><description>Ensure compliance with investigator's obligations re disclosure</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA29</code><description>Consider if case suitable for referral to Financial Investigation Unit and CPS for asset recovery eg confiscation order</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA3</code><description>Audio record interview unless exempt</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA4</code><description>PNC recordable</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA5</code><description>Submit a crime report</description></investigatoraction></investigatoractions><policeandcpschargingresponsibilities>D27968</policeandcpschargingresponsibilities><notes>(i) Prohibited conduct means conduct from which it may reasonably be concluded that the person intends to try the issue otherwise than on the basis of the evidence presented in the proceedings on the issue.&lt;br /&gt;(ii) An offence under this section is committed whether or not the person knows that the conduct is prohibited conduct.&lt;br /&gt;(iii) This offence should not be used if a juror has carried out research on the case or disclosed information to another juror; in such instances H12085 (CJS Code JY74011) or H12086 (CJS Code JY74012) should be used.</notes></english><indictment><indictmentindicator><code>N</code><description>No</description></indictmentindicator><structuredindictmentindicator><code>N</code><description>No</description></structuredindictmentindicator></indictment><other><powersofarrest>Arrest without warrant</powersofarrest><modeoftrial><code>IND</code><description>INDICTABLE</description></modeoftrial><consents><consent><code>A</code><description>Attorney General</description></consent></consents><timelimitforprosecutions>None</timelimitforprosecutions><penalty>Indictment: Two years imprisonment and / or a fine.Time limit for prosecutions:&lt;br /&gt;None</penalty><geographicregion><code>EW</code><description>England and Wales</description></geographicregion></other><codes><cjsoffencecode>JY74013</cjsoffencecode><recordableonpncindicator><code>Y</code><description>Yes</description></recordableonpncindicator><notifiabletoho><code>Y</code><description>Yes</description></notifiabletoho><hoclassification>079/08</hoclassification><mopireviewgroup><code>C</code><description>Group 3</description></mopireviewgroup><mopinoteslink>D19586</mopinoteslink><disqualificationclass><code>N</code><description>discretionary disqualification not endorsable</description></disqualificationclass><seatbeltoffence><code>N</code><description>No</description></seatbeltoffence><fptissuedbypolice>0</fptissuedbypolice><fptgraduated>0</fptgraduated><fptgraduatedhigh>0</fptgraduatedhigh><pndissuedbypolice>0</pndissuedbypolice><pndissuedbylocalauthorities>0</pndissuedbylocalauthorities><pndissuedbyothers>0</pndissuedbyothers><roadsidedeposits><code>N</code><description>No</description></roadsidedeposits></codes><libra><cjsoffencecategory><code>CI</code><description>Indictable</description></cjsoffencecategory><fineindicator><code>Y</code><description>Yes</description></fineindicator><maxfinetypecrownct><code>U</code><description>Unlimited</description></maxfinetypecrownct><custodialindicator><code>Y</code><description>Yes</description></custodialindicator><maxcustodialsentenceunitcrownct><code>Years</code><description>Years</description></maxcustodialsentenceunitcrownct><maxcustodialsentencelengthcrownct>2</maxcustodialsentencelengthcrownct><miscode><code>XXX</code><description>Other indictable offence</description></miscode></libra><ancillary><offencestartdate>2015-04-13</offencestartdate><datecreated>2015-05-14</datecreated><auditofamendme